Kind: ablation
Issue: #977
Takes out: the store that enables the message: pci_msi_arm() writes the address and the data and leaves MSI disabled, so the function goes on using its pin.  The boot's plain-MSI test reads the control word back without the enable bit, rings edu, and no message arrives on the slot.
Run: --edu --entry 14 600 -smp 4
Expect: plain MSI: edu was asked to raise .* WRONG, the capability is written and the device.s message did not arrive on its slot

diff --git a/uros/src/mach_kernel/x86_64/cpu/pci_msi.c b/uros/src/mach_kernel/x86_64/cpu/pci_msi.c
index 41f66c2e..d38528ba 100644
--- a/uros/src/mach_kernel/x86_64/cpu/pci_msi.c
+++ b/uros/src/mach_kernel/x86_64/cpu/pci_msi.c
@@ -111,7 +111,7 @@ pci_msi_arm(const struct pci_msi *m, uint64_t address, uint32_t data)
 	pci_cfg_command(m->segment, m->bus, m->dev, m->func,
 			PCI_CMD_BUS_MASTER, 0);
 
-	msi_control_write(m, (uint16_t)(control | PCI_MSI_CTL_ENABLE));
+	msi_control_write(m, control);	/* 977-msi-not-enabled: written, never enabled */
 	return 1;
 }
 
